 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "title": "Core Agents",
   "items": [
    "Both Advocates run in parallel and file separate Submissions to the Case store",
    "The Judge reads sealed evidence, both Submissions and Policy; History is filtered from its prompt",
    "After the outcome is fixed, code may lower Confidence or add a review trigger; History never changes the outcome or proves wrongdoing",
    "With no review trigger, Outcome is final automatically; a held proposal goes to a Human Reviewer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "violet",
   "title": "Supporting Features",
   "items": [
    "Supporting model and code features are switch-controlled; all off leaves the three Core Agents",
    "Escalation defaults on in demo config (no console checkbox); when enabled, Confidence below 0.70 or an amount above SGD 50 can hold a Ruling",
    "Safety Incidents always require human review; existing Policy or History triggers can also hold a proposal",
    "A reviewer confirms, or overrides with a reason; only an enabled Learning Loop receives overrides"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "amber",
   "title": "Simulated",
   "items": [
    "Trips, chat, fares, photos, policy and past Rulings are mock data",
    "Outcomes are shown on screen, not sent to anyone",
    "A payment is only ever recommended, never executed"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "slate",
   "title": "One store, one log",
   "items": [
    "Evidence, including History, is collected and sealed before Advocate submissions begin",
    "History stays in the Case but is withheld from Advocate and Judge prompts; post-outcome code consumes it",
    "Each Advocate files a Submission to the Case store before the Judge runs",
    "Every Case-store write appends a Communication Log event"
   ]
  }
 ]
}